{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22722075","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.22722075","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.22722075","identifiers":[{"identifier":"oai:zenodo.org:22722075","identifierType":"oai"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"oai","alternateIdentifier":"oai:zenodo.org:22722075"}],"creators":[{"name":"Jayadevan, Achyuth","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Achyuth","familyName":"Jayadevan","affiliation":["Manipal Institute of Technology, MAHE"],"nameIdentifiers":[{"nameIdentifier":"0009-0008-8745-4078","nameIdentifierScheme":"ORCID"}]}],"titles":[{"title":"Failure of finite isolated generation for an irreducible centralizer over a polycyclic group"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"Kourovka Problem 14.22"},{"subject":"Algebraic geometry over groups"},{"subject":"Polycyclic groups"},{"subject":"Radicals"},{"subject":"Nullstellensatz"},{"subject":"Lean 4"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-09-12","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":"en","types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsVersionOf","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.22722074","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1.0.0","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"},{"rights":"Copyright © 2026 Achyuth Jayadevan.","rightsUri":"http://rightsstatements.org/vocab/InC/1.0/"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Let \\(G=\\mathbb Z^2\\rtimes_M\\mathbb Z\\), where \\(M=\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}2\u00261\\\\1\u00261\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)\\), and let \\(t\\) generate the cyclic factor. The equation \\([x,t]=1\\) defines an infinite irreducible algebraic set over the two-generated torsion-free polycyclic group \\(G\\leq\\mathrm{SL}_3(\\mathbb Z)\\). We prove that its radical in \\(G*\\langle x\\rangle\\) is not the normal isolated closure of any finite subset. Thus no finite equivalent system has radical equal to its normal isolated closure, giving a negative answer to Problem 14.22 of the Kourovka Notebook. The proof identifies the radical as the kernel of a scalar Laurent collection homomorphism. Alternating bilinear extensions then provide torsion-free separating groups for arbitrary finite families of radical equations.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722075","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-09-12T10:15:23.000Z","registered":"2026-09-12T10:15:23.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-09-12T10:15:23.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22722075","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22722074","type":"dois"}]}}}}